    "content": "Whether you're a new grad walking into your first solo scan or an experienced sonographer who wants a faster reference than flipping through a textbook, SonoBuddy was built for you.\n\n## What Is SonoBuddy?\n\nSonoBuddy is a Progressive Web App (PWA) designed to give sonographers instant, phone-in-pocket access to the clinical information they need — right in the scan room.\n\nNo account required. No subscription wall. No loading spinner. Just open it and go.\n\n## What's Inside\n\n### Measurement Tables\n\nNormal and abnormal reference values for:\n\n- **Vascular** — carotid IMT, aorta, IVC, portal vein, renal artery doppler\n- **Abdominal** — liver, spleen, kidneys, gallbladder, pancreas\n- **OB/GYN** — uterus, ovaries, follicles, fetal biometry\n- **Thyroid** — gland dimensions, nodule size thresholds\n- **Cardiac** — basic echo measurements\n\nEvery measurement includes a clinical note so you understand *why* the threshold matters, not just what the number is.\n\n### Exam Protocols\n\nStep-by-step scanning guides with probe selection tips, key images to capture for PACS, and a full report checklist. Protocols currently include:\n\n- Carotid duplex\n- Lower extremity venous DVT survey\n- Abdominal aorta\n- Renal artery doppler\n- Abdominal complete\n- OB first trimester\n\n### Clinical Calculators\n\nBuilt-in calculators that return instant, color-coded results:\n\n- **ABI** (Ankle-Brachial Index) with PAD severity grading\n- **Resistive Index** with renal interpretation\n- **Carotid Stenosis** grading (SRU 2003 criteria)\n- **Organ Volume** (ellipsoid formula)\n- **AFI** (Amniotic Fluid Index)\n- **Gestational Age & EDD** from LMP or CRL\n- **Thyroid Volume**\n\n### Pathology Library\n\nConcise cards for the most common pathologies you'll encounter — ultrasound findings, red flags, differentials, and practical reporting tips.\n\n## Why We Built It\n\nNew sonography graduates told us the same thing over and over: *\"I keep a stack of papers in my pocket because I can't find anything fast enough mid-scan.\"*\n\nExisting apps either cost money, require an account, or are built for physicians rather than the person holding the probe. SonoBuddy is purpose-built for sonographers, with a UI designed for one-handed use in a darkened scan room.\n\n## What's Next\n\nSonoBuddy is actively being developed. Coming soon:\n\n- More protocols (OB anatomy survey, penile duplex, portal hypertension workup)\n- Expanded pathology library with annotated images\n- Favorites — pin the measurements and protocols you use every day\n- Enhanced offline mode\n\n---\n\n*SonoBuddy is a reference tool, not a diagnostic authority. All clinical decisions should involve the ordering provider and interpreting physician.*"
